From 5358b4cb3693511391c6562313e49574cb9b0243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayush Das <das.ayush4890@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 09:58:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: PORT fallback, configurable compile timeout, real error
 logging
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- server.config.js: PORT had no fallback, so `npm run dev` without a .env
  started the server on `undefined`. Docker sets PORT so this only bit bare
  local runs. Now `process.env.PORT || 3000`.
- latex.service.js: COMPILE_TIMEOUT_MS was hardcoded to 15s while the README
  documented 30s. Made it env-configurable (COMPILE_TIMEOUT_MS) and raised the
  default to 60s — xelatex/fontspec templates routinely exceed 15s on a cold
  run and were being SIGKILLed mid-compile.
- latex.controller.js: the 422 branch logged the fixed string
  'invalid respone from controleer', discarding the compile log and the parsed
  error list that had just been extracted. Now logs both, so a failed compile
  is diagnosable from the service logs instead of only from the HTTP response.
